o attacks f6/g7/c7/d6/f10/g9 (offboard), so it directly checks the king on c7 (yes, e8 attacks c7). This is a strong forcing move.\n\nReason: Playing N: d6-e8 gives immediate check to the black king, forcing a response and keeping initiative against the exposed king. It also jumps deeper, potentially setting up follow-up forks/captures while limiting Black’s ability to consolidate.\n\nAnswer: N: d6-e8'}
